    {
      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.CompactWeakPoissonSobolev.compact_weak_poisson_sobolev",
      "title": "Actual compact weak Poisson: complex Schwartz, TD and Sobolev",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
          "label": "PBPS AppendixC.1 authored analytic prerequisite",
          "scope": "Derive actual all-complex-Schwartz tested PDE with both products L1, genuine complex volume-L2 classes/AE embeddings, actual TD Laplacian and MemSobolev2 using B2=I-(2pi)^-2 Delta. Genuine conditional same originalD before epsilon/f, one actualu before allC2 compactcutoffs; retain parent properties. No real mixed-second representatives/Hessian, original weighted localized-domain membership/core/Bochner, BL/Poincare/epsilon0/measurable fiber selector/full4.1/main/composition. Reflected/RGO laws/operators/scales distinct; TV does not transfer unbounded cost."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.CompactWeakPoissonSobolev"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "E is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with Borel measurable structure and canonical full-space volume, including dimension zero. v and F are real pointwise functions with genuine global volume MemLp2; K is compact and tsupport v and tsupport F are contained in K.",
        "For every real C2 compact phi, v*Delta phi and F*phi are integrable for volume and integral v*Delta phi=integral F*phi. This generic analytic interface is consumed with these inputs actually derived by the same-D localized resolvent; no all-Schwartz, TD equation or final Sobolev certificate is supplied.",
        "All rough functions/class representatives are differentiated only as distributions. Complex test derivatives are real Frechet derivatives on E, real/imaginary projections are real-linear CLMs, and the complex TD pairing is bilinear integral psi*v without conjugation. No Nontrivial or positive-dimensional assumption is added."
      ],
      "statement": "Under the exact ordinary-volume global L2/support and real compact-C2 PDE assumptions, Construct actual vc,Fc in complex L2(volume), with vc=volume-a.e. ofReal(v) and Fc=volume-a.e. ofReal(F). For every complex Schwartz psi, both (Delta psi)*ofReal(v) and psi*ofReal(F) are L1 and their integrals equal. For T_v=Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc) and T_F=Lp.toTemperedDistribution(Fc), derive Delta T_v=T_F and MemSobolev 2 2 T_v. The latter uses B2 T=T-(2pi)^(-2) Delta T and a genuine complex L2 witness, not a supplied regularity result.",
      "formula": "v,F\\in L^2(dx),\\ \\operatorname{tsupp}(v),\\operatorname{tsupp}(F)\\subseteq K;\\quad\\int v\\Delta\\varphi=\\int F\\varphi\\ (\\varphi\\in C_c^2)\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ \\Delta T_v=T_F,\\quad B_2T_v=T_v-(2\\pi)^{-2}T_F\\in\\operatorname{LpTD}(L^2),\\quad T_v\\in H^2_{\\rm Bessel}.",
      "boundary": "Derive actual all-complex-Schwartz tested PDE with both products L1, genuine complex volume-L2 classes/AE embeddings, actual TD Laplacian and MemSobolev2 using B2=I-(2pi)^-2 Delta. Genuine conditional same originalD before epsilon/f, one actualu before allC2 compactcutoffs; retain parent properties. No real mixed-second representatives/Hessian, original weighted localized-domain membership/core/Bochner, BL/Poincare/epsilon0/measurable fiber selector/full4.1/main/composition. Reflected/RGO laws/operators/scales distinct; TV does not transfer unbounded cost.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Enclose the actual supports with one smooth outer plateau",
          "text": "Use compactness to choose a positive inner radius enclosing K strictly. The actual unnormalized smooth bump theta has larger outer radius, compact support and equals1 in a neighborhood of each x in K. No normalized mollifier, tail limit, derivative-bound certificate or positive-dimension premise is used.",
          "formula": "K\\subset B(0,R),\\quad\\theta\\in C_c^\\infty,\\quad\\theta=1\\ \\text{near every }x\\in K.",
          "lean": "outer_cutoff; Bornology.IsBounded.subset_ball_lt; ContDiffBump.eventuallyEq_one_of_mem_ball"
        },
        {
          "title": "Actually extend real tests to every complex Schwartz test",
          "text": "For arbitrary psi test the given real PDE with theta*Re psi and theta*Im psi. These are genuine C2 compact tests. Laplacian locality and real-linear CLM composition derive Delta(theta Re psi)=Re(Delta psi) on K, and likewise imaginary part; outside K the actual v/F are zero. The same theta/K works independently of psi.",
          "formula": "\\int v\\operatorname{Re}(\\Delta\\psi)=\\int F\\operatorname{Re}\\psi,\\qquad\\int v\\operatorname{Im}(\\Delta\\psi)=\\int F\\operatorname{Im}\\psi.",
          "lean": "real_schwartz_component; laplacian_congr_nhds; ContDiffAt.laplacian_CLM_comp_left; image_eq_zero_of_notMem_tsupport"
        },
        {
          "title": "Prove legal complex products before combining integrals",
          "text": "Actual global volume L2, MemLp.ofReal and Schwartz L2 of psi and Delta psi yield both bilinear products L1 through Holder2/2/1. Only then integral_re/integral_im and Complex.ext combine the genuine real equalities. There is no complex conjugation or conjugated inner-product substitution.",
          "formula": "\\int(\\Delta\\psi)(v:\\mathbb C)=\\int\\psi(F:\\mathbb C),\\quad(\\Delta\\psi)v,\\psi F\\in L^1(dx).",
          "lean": "complex_schwartz_pde; MemLp.integrable_mul; integral_re; integral_im; Complex.ext"
        },
        {
          "title": "Build and identify actual AE-linked L2 distributions",
          "text": "Build vc/Fc using actual complex MemLp.toLp. State their volume-AE equalities explicitly before each integral transfer. The genuine LpTD pairing is integral psi*vc. Its distribution Laplacian acts on Delta psi with positive sign, giving Delta T_v=T_F by extensionality on all complex Schwartz tests; no class-support claim is made for the selected quotient representatives.",
          "formula": "v_C=_{dx\\text{-ae}}(v:\\mathbb C),\\quad F_C=_{dx\\text{-ae}}(F:\\mathbb C),\\quad\\Delta T_v=T_F.",
          "lean": "actual_tempered_laplacian; MemLp.coeFn_toLp; Lp.toTemperedDistribution_apply; TemperedDistribution.laplacian_apply_apply"
        },
        {
          "title": "Construct the Fourier-normalized Bessel witness",
          "text": "Order2 Bessel multiplier is 1+norm(x)^2. The pinned Fourier Laplacian is -(2pi)^2 times the norm-square multiplier. Actual multiplier linearity and real-to-complex scalar cancellation derive B2 T=T-(2pi)^(-2) Delta T. The complex L2 class vc-(a:complex)*Fc witnesses the definition, equivalently using the true L2 embeddings and their subtraction/scalar linearity.",
          "formula": "a=(2\\pi)^{-2},\\quad B_2T_v=\\operatorname{LpTD}(v_C-aF_C),\\quad\\mathrm{MemSobolev}\\ 2\\ 2\\ T_v.",
          "lean": "bessel_two_identity; laplacian_eq_fourierMultiplierCLM; sobolev_of_compact_pde; memSobolev_zero_iff; MemSobolev.sub; MemSobolev.smul"
        },
        {
          "title": "Return this exact interface and retain its boundary",
          "text": "Return the actual classes, AE links, both complex integrabilities/all-Schwartz equation, TD Laplacian and Bessel-Sobolev membership. Dimension0 needs no unit vector or division by dimension. Real mixed-second representatives/Hessian, original weighted closure-domain/core and Bochner extension are separate next producers; neither BL/Poincare nor a source main theorem follows here.",
          "formula": "\\text{actual complex Bessel-Sobolev interface};\\quad\\text{real Hessian/core/BL remain open}.",
          "lean": "compact_weak_poisson_sobolev"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Under the exact ordinary-volume global L2/support and real compact-C2 PDE assumptions, Construct actual vc,Fc in complex L2(volume), with vc=volume-a.e. ofReal(v) and Fc=volume-a.e. ofReal(F). For every complex Schwartz psi, both (Delta psi)*ofReal(v) and psi*ofReal(F) are L1 and their integrals equal. For T_v=Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc) and T_F=Lp.toTemperedDistribution(Fc), derive Delta T_v=T_F and MemSobolev 2 2 T_v. The latter uses B2 T=T-(2pi)^(-2) Delta T and a genuine complex L2 witness, not a supplied regularity result.",
      "lean_proof": "Enclose the actual supports with one smooth outer plateau; Actually extend real tests to every complex Schwartz test; Prove legal complex products before combining integrals; Build and identify actual AE-linked L2 distributions; Construct the Fourier-normalized Bessel witness; Return this exact interface and retain its boundary",
